    Velociraptors were indeed most interesting creatures.  They were bipedal
with reasonable overlap of the visual fields of their eyes (giving them
moderate binocular vision), they had high brain/body mass ratio among
reptiles, they indeed seem to have been pack hunters (one paleontological
find seems to be several of them -- or perhaps it is the related species
_Deinonychus_ (which I probably can't spell) grouped around a prey animal
which they had just slain), and some authorities think they had an opposable
"thumb" -- the outermost of the three "digits" on each forelimb.

