You mean they changed the dating *again*?   Sigh...it's getting so you can't
even keep up with the *past* any more!  :-)

I'm very suspicious of simple diffusionism.  It's too neat.  *My* favorite
interpretation of the (scanty) evidence is that pastoralism evolved separately
from farming, probably earlier, and quite possibly among nomads in the
circumpolar region (not an original idea; I got it from Joseph Campbell).
On this view, the first dairyers were probably people culturally (if not
genetically) much like the Lapp reindeer-herders.
