Quoth Eric S. Raymond, verily I saith unto thee:
> 
> > Interestingly enough in this connection, I came across a mention a while
> > back that a particular American Indian language, I believe either Navajo or
> > Hopi, used the same word to indicate both blue and green.
> 
> That's quite common.  Some languages have as few as *two* color words.
> There's a hierarchy of color distinctions such that if a language has color
> distinction A from B, then it has distinction X from Y.  Turns out the
> blue/green distinction is the "last" to get made ("warm vs. cool" is the first).

Yes indeed.  Welsh is a good example, having (esp. in Literary Welsh)
several words more-or-less for blue, but which can also cover all sorts of
greens and greys and other hues.  Even English does this to a certain
extent with metaphorical colour names, such as "sea" colour.  Is it blue
or green?


